<h1>Pensions and social care: assessing a reported trade-off</h1>

<p class="lede">In September 2026 news reports linked two things: a less generous yearly increase in the State Pension, and free social care for adults in England. This page sets out what has been decided, what has been proposed and what has only been reported. It then lists the questions any such trade-off would have to answer.</p>

{% call m.note("The position on the morning of " ~ (news.as_of | displayDate), 2) %}
<p>This page was checked before the Prime Minister's speech to his party conference on {{ news.as_of | timeTag | safe }}. {{ m.c("speech-not-yet-given") }} Reports of what the speech would say are reports, not a record of what was said. We found no published proposal to replace the triple lock in order to pay for social care. That can change quickly. Treat this page as a dated record.</p>
{% endcall %}

